GET {{plainHost}}/anything/no-scheme

::: post
test("a URL without a scheme is sent over http", () => {
  expect(res.status).toBe(200);
  expect(res.json().scheme).toBe("http");
  expect(res.json().path).toBe("/anything/no-scheme");
});

::: docs
`plainHost` has no scheme, like typing `localhost:8080` in the URL bar: Postino sends it over
`http://`. Plain HTTP in either environment, so it never carries a certificate warning.
